  {
   "heading": "This, that: ce, cet, cette, ces",
   "body": "To point at something, use a demonstrative instead of the article:\n\n- *ce* + masculine noun: *ce livre* (this / that book)\n- *cet* + masculine noun starting with a vowel or silent h: *cet ordinateur*, *cet homme*\n- *cette* + feminine noun: *cette montre*\n- *ces* + any plural noun: *ces clés*, *ces livres*\n\nNote *cet* and *cette* sound the same: /sɛt/. To insist on \"this one here\" or \"that one there\", add *-ci* or *-là*: *ce livre-ci*, *ce livre-là*."
  }
 ],
